      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "The following example shows how to determine whether a given region is equal to the region that’s displaying on the map.",
      "normalizedSource": "The following example shows how to determine whether a given region is equal to the region that’s displaying on the map.",
      "sourceHash": "b70e5b49cf12b0a8d5332404a59bf867732f2e613a94e6877f134131d447787f",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Discussion",
      "contextAfter": "```javascript\n// Create a map.\nconst map = new mapkit.Map(\"my-map-element-id\");\n\n// Create a region named myRegion.\nconst coordinate = new mapkit.Coordinate(37.415, -122.048333); // latitude, longitude\nconst span = new mapkit.CoordinateSpan(.016, .016); // latitude delta, longitude delta\nconst myRegion = new mapkit.CoordinateRegion(coordinate, span);\n\n// Check whether myRegion is equal to the current map region.\nif (myRegion.equals(map.region))\n   console.log(\"These two regions are equal.\");\n\n```",
      "documentTitle": "equals(anotherRegion)",
      "framework": "MapKitJS",
